==Trivia==
* This card's immersive illustration includes {{p|Golisopod}}, {{p|Masquerain}}, {{p|Pinsir}}, [[Plumeria]], {{p|Salazzle}}, {{p|Fomantis}}, {{rf|Alolan}} {{p|Grimer}}, and two {{tc|Team Skull Grunt}}s.
* This card's effect is identical to that of {{TCG ID|Flashfire|Startling Megaphone|97}} in the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]], but this card is a {{TCGP|Supporter card}} instead of an {{TCGP|Item card}}.
** {{TCG|Guzma}} also exists in the Pokémon Trading Card Game, but with a different effect.
* The {{rar/TCGP|Star|3}} prints of this card and {{TCG ID|Celestial Guardians|Lillie|209}} are the first {{TCGP|immersive card|immersive}} {{TCGP|Supporter card}}s in the game; all immersive cards released prior had been {{TCG|Pokémon}} cards. Only Lillie was revealed in pre-release announcements and trailers.

===Origin===
* [[Guzma]] is the leader of [[Team Skull]], which appears as the [[villainous team]] in {{game4|7}}.

